WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.018
Theater Module Introduction.

2
00:00:03.018 --> 00:00:06.251
GENAI 101 - Module 2: Theater.

3
00:00:06.251 --> 00:00:12.718
Presented by Idowu David Awoyemi, The University of Alabama.

4
00:00:13.318 --> 00:00:15.506
Welcome to the theater module.

5
00:00:15.506 --> 00:00:17.622
Four lessons, four artifacts.

6
00:00:17.622 --> 00:00:28.713
In lesson two point one, you'll draft a two-character scene
with a text model, direct two rounds of revision, and
rewrite a third of the lines yourself.

7
00:00:28.713 --> 00:00:35.425
In two point two, you'll score a monologue into beats and
build an avatar performance of it.

8
00:00:35.425 --> 00:00:42.065
In two point three, you'll choreograph a short movement
piece from generated video phrases.

9
00:00:42.065 --> 00:00:52.791
And in two point four, you'll evaluate AI feedback on your
own scene and take a position on whether you would stage AI-
assisted work with students.

10
00:00:53.391 --> 00:00:57.319
The competencies map the same way they did in music.

11
00:00:57.319 --> 00:01:05.174
Storytelling is prompt engineering and creativity: a scene
brief, director's notes, and a human rewrite.

12
00:01:05.174 --> 00:01:14.011
Avatar performance is computational thinking: decomposing a
speech into beats and sequencing four variables per beat.

13
00:01:14.011 --> 00:01:23.830
Choreography is problem solving: text-to-video is the least
reliable tool in the course, so you'll diagnose failures and
fix them.

14
00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:27.305
And the final lesson is evaluation and ethics.

15
00:01:27.905 --> 00:01:33.075
If you completed the music module, you'll recognize the
moves.

16
00:01:33.075 --> 00:01:35.910
Write a brief before you generate.

17
00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:38.161
Change one thing at a time.

18
00:01:38.161 --> 00:01:42.080
Evaluate against criteria you named in advance.

19
00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.414
Credit the tool.

20
00:01:43.414 --> 00:01:47.333
Theater changes the vocabulary, not the method.

21
00:01:47.333 --> 00:01:57.340
Objective and obstacle replace tempo and instrumentation;
director's notes replace prompt revisions; beats replace
bars.

22
00:01:57.940 --> 00:01:59.924
One thing before you start.

23
00:01:59.924 --> 00:02:06.023
Theater happens between people in a room, and nothing in
this module replaces that.

24
00:02:06.023 --> 00:02:17.119
The tools help you draft faster, visualize staging before
you have a cast, rehearse without a partner, and give
students a way to see their ideas move.

25
00:02:17.119 --> 00:02:21.895
Every lesson asks how the artifact returns to the rehearsal
room.

26
00:02:21.895 --> 00:02:28.729
Keep a Theater Module Notes document with every prompt you
use and one line about the result.

27
00:02:28.729 --> 00:02:31.154
Let's go to lesson two point one.
